 "summary": "The theorem proves Bolzano–Weierstrass in any proper pseudometric space. If a sequence x lies in a bounded set s, then some strictly increasing reindexing φ makes x∘φ converge to a point a in closure s. Every ℝⁿ is a proper metric space, so this generalizes the paper's statement. There is no substantive caveat: the Lean statement is at least as strong as the paper's.",
 "glossary": [
